# class: layer-name
# note: F.Cu given the user name TOP in the layer table alone: KiCad loads and passes it (F10, the control until AET-WO-3303), but a copper row is read by its canonical name only, so every gate that reads the board refuses it (AET-WO-3303 §1.4)
# main: drc 0 pass; drc-parity 0 pass; extract 0 pass
# drc: 0 pass
# drc-parity: 3 LayersDisagree
# extract: 3 LayersDisagree
@@ find
		(0 "F.Cu" signal)
@@ replace
		(0 "F.Cu" signal "TOP")
@@ end
